#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:6
#: 9646c5364e2745fc83d83bf7a6d1a462
msgid "Inclusion and Exclusion Fences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:9
#: 88644ea62c12492da0dc9094e5c200c8
msgid "Overview"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:11
#: 696099f277cc4d58812890a42d9eb458
msgid "ArduPilot includes support for polygon fences with up to 70 points and for pure circular fences with specified radii. Unlike the home-based cylindrical fence :ref:`cylindrical fence <common-ac2_simple_geofence>`, the circular inclusion/exclusion fence can be placed anywhere. Either the polygonal or circular fences may be selected to be inclusion or exclusion type, and may be mixed. The purpose of these fences are to attempt to stop your vehicle from flying into (exclusion), or out of (inclusion), the fences by initiating a failsafe action like RTL (See :ref:`FENCE_ACTION<FENCE_ACTION>`) or, if flying in Loiter mode for Copter and :ref:`common-object-avoidance-landing-page` is setup, the vehicle will normally stop before breaching the fence and in some cases, plan paths around the boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:13
#: 88771584cea244258c4cb798123ce1e0
msgid "This feature is an extension of the simpler home-based :ref:`cylindrical fence <common-ac2_simple_geofence>` and can be combined with it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:15
#: f8453552708a4c2f8b5eb20f842f3c2d
msgid "While Copter and Rover can use :ref:`common-object-avoidance-landing-page` strategies to avoid most fence breaches, Plane only has airborne aircraft :ref:`ADSB avoidance <common-ads-b-receiver>`. For safety, plan your polygon fences anticipating the path of whatever :ref:`FENCE_ACTION<FENCE_ACTION>` is selected upon breach. This usually means significantly larger fence boundaries than what is being protected."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:17
#: 63b5995b0ac14eb79c5cc827711eba76
msgid "You can have multiple circular or polygon inclusion or exclusion fences, all active at the same time. The example PLAN screen from Mission Planner, below, shows examples of each. Note that they can overlap, with one another. So in the example below the Plane could fly within the union of the large polygonal fence AND within the circular overlapping fence without breaching. The example below is not realistic, since with the large inclusion fence, the outside exclusion fences would never be reached and are superfluous, but it shows all the different kinds of fences that can be created."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:22
#: 09292daa06794f638efb5111ff877278
msgid "See :ref:`common-geofencing-landing-page` for fence setup parameters common to all fences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:24
#: 80401b1c3faf4e929c5b5f1516c8fe42
msgid "These fences are created and treated in a similar way to mission command lists and rally point lists and loaded into the autopilot. Each item in the list specifies a point in the polygonal boundary or a circular item, whether its inclusion or exclusion type, and radius if circular. Most GCS provide a graphical drawing facility to add in the design of the fence boundaries and inclusion/exclusion type."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:26
#: ae759eebf6564f6e8a4d5105eb884cb3
msgid "Multiple fences can be specified of differing types and shapes in the list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:33
#: e167880c1c7546dcb2d3474d3b3a57e0
msgid "Number of fences"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:35
#: b1462159dcd5457fa3828ed957ab1953
msgid "Fences are stored in a separate reserved area of flash in the autopilot from mission items and rally points. The number that can be stored depends on their complexity, but when you go to \"Write\" them to the autopilot, an error message will be displayed if storage limit is exceeded. In this case, you can enable storage on the SD Card by setting the :ref:`BRD_SD_FENCE<BRD_SD_FENCE>` parameter to a non-zero size, which will store the fences on SD card instead of internal memory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:39
#: 13243ab37b914d23aff04009f8c770b2
msgid "Other Warnings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:41
#: 5de8571552014888846165f47722c51b
msgid "The minimum recommended fence radius is 30m"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:42
#: b9ef300947d4486b860ed0a783937ee1
msgid "The fence requires the GPS to be functioning well so do not disable the :ref:`GPS arming check <common-prearm-safety-checks>` nor the :ref:`EKF failsafe <ekf-inav-failsafe>` while the fence is enabled. Conversely, if you disable either of these checks, disable the Fence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:45
#: f2afc3a3274649dcb3bf17d4ab73a50f
msgid "For the best results, ensure RTL is working on your vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:46
#: 6d8951b2a4db451ba39570613f9f7ccd
msgid "With the Fence enabled in Copter and Rover, the pre-arm checks will require you have GPS lock before arming the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:48
#: a5cc24c9c95045f694c2d73d2d41ecfa
msgid "In Copter, if EKF failsafe occurs and the Fence is enabled and you lose GPS lock while flying the fence will be disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:50
#: ba20e5ec284a4359a77ff9d0cf78194c
msgid "In Copter, if EKF failsafe occurs and the Fence is enabled and in an autonomous mode, the vehicle will switch to LAND (HOLD for Rover) because we no longer know the vehicle position and we want to ensure the vehicle never travels far outside the fence. If this is not desired, the pilot can retake control by moving the flight mode switch to a manual mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:54
#: 1688b97cddfe428ab60560ea72304e0b
msgid "The Copter and Rover backup fences are created 20m out from the previous breached fence not 20m out from the vehicle's position.  This means if you choose to override the fence you may have less than 20m to regain vehicle control before the fence switches the vehicle to the :ref:`FENCE_ACTION<FENCE_ACTION>` again.  If you really want to override the fence, you should be ready to switch the flight mode twice or alternatively set-up the enable/disable fence switch."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:62
#: 8c5d463cb8544763ad82bf7f9a76e49c
msgid "You can define many inclusion and exclusion fences. However,multiple inclusions fences, including the :ref:`cylindrical fences <common-ac2_simple_geofence>` must overlap, since the vehicle can operate only within the complete overlap area of all of the inclusion fences. Exclusion fences may be placed within or outside of inclusion fences."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:64
#: 0a0fd570af3b4948af90107d000b477b
msgid "In order to upload or download these fences from Mission Planner the connected link must be using MAVLink2 protocol. Normally, since the USB connection is used, this protocol is default. However, radio linked connections may use MAVLink1 by default and would need to be changed to MAVLink2 in order to upload and download across them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:66
#: 0da01168dc95431a8cf2c752b87b65c4
msgid "You can have both the :ref:`cylindrical fences <common-ac2_simple_geofence>` and inclusion/exclusion fences and choose to use just the HOME centered \"tin-can\" for a flight by selecting only the \"Circle\" or \"Altitude and Circle\" for :ref:`FENCE_TYPE<FENCE_TYPE>`. You can chose to enable the :ref:`cylindrical fences <common-ac2_simple_geofence>`, these inclusion/exclusion fences, and/or altitude limit, in any combination, with this parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:69
#: 03ecafcf95c242fd8330eae5bb11c629
msgid "Combining with the Cylindrical Fence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:71
#: eab2b11af81344ab942b27f7ec6fa91d
msgid "A polygon fence can be used in combination with the :ref:`cylindrical fences <common-ac2_simple_geofence>` and the failsafe behaviour (i.e. stop at the fence or RTL) will trigger at whichever barrier the vehicle reaches first (i.e. the green line shown below)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-polygon_fence.rst:77
#: d194a92599fb439c96e4875f7f63c4bf
msgid "Please see the :ref:`Cylindrical Fence <common-ac2_simple_geofence>` page for additional warnings and instructions including how to enable/disable the fence with the RC channel auxiliary switches."
msgstr ""
